{"tool_name":"saspector","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"saspector","home":"https://github.com/LoGT-KULeuven/SASpector","license":"MIT","summary":"Analysis of missing genomic regions in draft genomes of prokaryotes.","addition_date":"2022-07-25T01:06:32.578763Z","last_update_date":"2022-07-25T01:06:32.581285Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:saspector","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"cedric.lood@kuleuven.be","name":"C\u00e9dric Lood","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7826-3378","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"vera.vannoort@kuleuven.be","name":"Vera van Noort","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Alejandro Correa Rojo"},{"name":"Deniz Sinar"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Parsing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_1812"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"de Novo sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3644"},{"term":"k-mer counting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3472"}]}],"name":"SASpector","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAC208","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022 The Author(s). Published by Oxford University Press.Missing regions in short-read assemblies of prokaryote genomes are often attributed to biases in sequencing technologies and to repetitive elements, the former resulting in low sequencing coverage of certain loci and the latter to unresolved loops in the de novo assembly graph. We developed SASpector, a command-line tool that compares short-read assemblies (draft genomes) to their corresponding closed assemblies and extracts missing regions to analyze them at the sequence and functional level. SASpector allows to benchmark the need for resolved genomes, can be integrated into pipelines to control the quality of assemblies, and could be 